      "disposition": "exact_action_ineligible",
      "rationale": "Roy amendment6 (separate Clerk ordinal3) adds NEPA111 definition16 of significant effect as proximate and concrete harm directly caused by proposed agency action materially impairing human health or property, and replaces102(2)(C) detailed-statement trigger with at least one significant effect/environmental impact statement. Both h and i are complete; RH page23 line13 insertion and material4332/4336e baselines distinguish proposed change. Not only a terminology edit or all environmental review abolished; health/property harms are statutory predicates, not observed effects or immigration programme criteria. Initial voice ayes, Huffman recorded-demand, actual postponement, resumed recorded-demand/order and own rejection remain distinct. Exact Foushee/Massie labels retained; no component-preference, motive, ideology, character, corruption, endorsement or voting recommendation inferred. Established member-neutral functional Immigration-domain exclusion candidate only, noncounting/unapproved; no new meaning, question, package, ontology or methodology.",
