    {
      "action_ids": [
        "house:119:1:356"
      ],
      "disposition": "exact_action_ineligible",
      "rationale": "Full passed H.R.4776 SPEED Act read, all sections1-4, rather than importing rejected amendments1/5/6 into passage. NEPA procedural purposes/equivalent State or Tribal review; qualified effects, research and applicant goals; document certainty/authorization and court/consent/violation/fraud/immediate-harm/request exceptions; concurrent reviews and qualified60/21/7/30 calendar clocks; programmatic5-to10-year change/reuse/categorical exclusions; major-action financial-control/farm-loan exceptions, reasonably foreseeable effects, CEQ energy duty; judicial deference,706(2)(A) remand not vacatur, conditional150-day/substantive-comment/direct-harm/categorical-exclusion limits, qualified Tribal-trust review exception, record/judgment/appeal clocks all retained. Section4 preserves ongoing agency administrative corrections initiated Jan20,2025 through enactment whether completed; H.Res953 adopts Report4 before floor amendments. No enacted/in-force claim, guaranteed permits/outcomes/timing/individual eligibility judgment, or interpretation of specific immigrant/border projects inferred from generally applicable environmental procedure. Own direct passage voice ayes, recorded yeas/nays demand/order and passage retained; no postponed question invented. Exact Foushee/Massie labels retained; no component-preference, motive, ideology, character, corruption, endorsement or voting recommendation inferred. Established member-neutral functional Immigration-domain exclusion candidate only, noncounting/unapproved; no new meaning, question, package, ontology or methodology.",
